Argument contracts
------------------
Argument positions are zero-based; types and exact selectors are in JSON.
Ordinary kernel errors are native errno, except where noted. No new probe
reads file contents, packet payloads, keys, passwords, pathnames or commands.
Pointers are opaque live identities. Never dereference a saved identity;
addresses and fds are reused. Pair synchronous calls by PID/thread/depth.
Asynchronous GEOM work must not be paired by thread. Process/thread exit,
cancellation, nonlocal exits and dropped events can leave unmatched starts.

pipe:::read-start/write-start/direct-start(pipe, requested_bytes)
pipe:::read-done/write-done/direct-done(pipe, residual_bytes, errno)
  Residual is uio_resid; requested minus residual measures uio progress,
  including possible partial progress on errors. Existing read/write probes
  retain their older byte-accounting contracts. Direct is a nested operation
  within a write; it need not consume the entire requested residual.
pipe:::resize-start(pipe, requested_size)
pipe:::resize-done(pipe, requested_size, errno)
  Requested size is not a promise of allocation on error.

kqueue:::scan-start(queue, maxevents)
kqueue:::scan-done(queue, selected_events, errno)
  Selected events need not have reached userspace if copyout failed. This
  covers kqueue_scan, not registration or the whole kevent syscall.
kqueue:::wait-start(queue); wait-done(queue, raw_msleep_status)
  Fires on each actual wait; includes raw ERESTART/EWOULDBLOCK before mapping.
kqueue:::copyout-start(queue, batch_events)
kqueue:::copyout-done(queue, batch_events, errno)
  Includes only scan batches, not EV_RECEIPT/change-list copyout.

clock:::timer-set-start(timer_id, flags); timer-set-done(timer_id, errno)
  Native kern_ktimer_settime, after syscall copyin and before syscall copyout.
vm:::fault-trap-start(map, fault_type, fault_flags)
vm:::fault-trap-done(map, Mach_KERN_status)
  Trap wrapper, not every vm_fault caller. No faulting address is recorded.
geom:::io-submit(bio, provider, command, length_bytes, direct_send)
  Before inline or queued dispatch; pair with the existing io-complete by
  live bio identity if desired. ENOMEM can cause retries/re-submission;
  do not interpret submit count as completed physical device I/O count.
ifnet:::ioctl-start(interface, command)
ifnet:::ioctl-done(interface, command, errno)
  Covers calls through if_ioctl(), not every legacy direct ifp->if_ioctl call.

usb:::drain-start(transfer, root); drain-done(transfer, root)
  Non-NULL usbd_transfer_drain only. Includes acquiring the transfer lock,
  stopping the transfer and waiting for outstanding callbacks. No errno.
pcm:::drain-start(channel); drain-done(channel, chn_sync_status)
  Around chn_sync in playback close. chn_flush continues to ignore that
  status, as before. This is not the whole PCM close operation.
nvme:::reset-start(controller); reset-done(controller, hw_reset_status)
  Around hardware reset in the reset task. Completion precedes controller
  restart/failure handling; zero does not prove successful later restart.
pci:::power-start(device, requested_state)
pci:::power-done(device, requested_state, errno)
  Includes no-op and validation outcomes, register write and mandated delay.
  Successful write/delay is not independent verification of device health.

linuxkpi_work:::delayed-cancel-start(delayed_work)
linuxkpi_work:::delayed-cancel-done(delayed_work, cancelled_boolean)
  Entire linux_cancel_delayed_work_sync retry loop. False is not errno.
linuxkpi_shrinker:::count-start(shrinker); count-done(shrinker, object_count)
linuxkpi_shrinker:::scan-start(shrinker, requested_batch)
linuxkpi_shrinker:::scan-done(shrinker, raw_unsigned_result)
  Callback results retain LinuxKPI conventions, including SHRINK_STOP.
  This does not repair or change the existing shrink-control algorithm.
linuxulator*:epoll::eventfd-create(initial_count, flags, fd_or_minus_one, errno)
linuxulator*:epoll::timerfd-create(linux_clock_id, flags, fd_or_minus_one, errno)
  Legacy eventfd (without the "2") is not included. Provider name/module
  follow the existing LIN_SDT macros: linuxulator/linuxulator32, epoll.
vfs:::syncer-start(vnode); syncer-done(vnode, fsync_errno)
  Only sync_vnode's lazy fsync callback. Errors remain ignored by its caller.
opencrypto:::session-start(driver_selection, session_mode)
opencrypto:::session-done(driver_selection, errno)
  Requested driver selection is not necessarily the selected driver ID.

fetchio*:::read-start(connection, requested_bytes)
fetchio*:::write-start(connection, requested_bytes)
fetchio*:::read-done/write-done(connection, signed_result, errno_or_zero)
  Write covers fetch_write, not direct fetch_writev calls. Read covers
  fetch_read, not reads satisfied entirely from another buffer. EOF is a
  zero result. Successful partial reads report zero error despite stale errno.
archiveio*:::skip-start(archive); skip-done(archive, ARCHIVE_status)
  Begins after archive_check_magic, which itself may return or abort.
threadwait*:::rwlock-start(lock_address, mode)
threadwait*:::rwlock-done(lock_address, mode, pthread_error)
  Mode 0=read, 1=write. Each slow helper invocation, not the fast path,
  validation errors, entire public API, or lock hold time. EINTR retries
  are distinct intervals. Userland retry acquisition can end the loop.
cpcopy*:::transfer-start(source_fd, target_fd)
cpcopy*:::transfer-done(source_fd, target_fd, bytes_written, errno_or_zero)
cpcopy*:::fallback(source_fd, target_fd, triggering_errno)
  Only the data loop. Excludes open, metadata preservation, close failures
  and link-only modes. EINTR retry is inside the interval; fallback switches
  to read/write on EINVAL exactly as before.
installcopy*:::range-start(source_fd, target_fd)
installcopy*:::range-done(source_fd, target_fd, signed_result, errno_or_zero)
installcopy*:::fallback(source_fd, target_fd, triggering_errno)
installcopy*:::sync-start(target_fd); sync-done(target_fd, errno_or_zero)
  Each copy_file_range attempt and safe fsync. Read/write fallback and digest
  loops are not individually probed. Bootstrap builds omit this provider.
semwait*:::park-start(usem_address, clock_id, flags)
semwait*:::park-done(usem_address, raw_return, errno_or_zero)
semwait*:::wake-start(usem_address)
semwait*:::wake-done(usem_address, raw_return, errno_or_zero)
  Raw _umtx_op calls, including those from libc's generated cancellation
  points. Excludes userland fast acquisition/post, validation and deferred
  cancellation after the raw wait. usem address is the internal _kern member,
  not the public sem_t address. A wake failure remains ignored by sem_post.

Installed base surface
----------------------
Component                   Destination / package
--------------------------  -----------------------------------------------
cp                          /bin/cp / runtime
install                     /usr/bin/install / runtime
libfetch                    /usr/lib/libfetch.so.6 / fetch
libarchive                  /usr/lib/libarchive.so.7 / libarchive
libthr                      /lib/libthr.so.3 / clibs
libc                        /lib/libc.so.7 / clibs
BSDInstruments profiles     /usr/share/bsdinstruments/profiles / bsdinstruments
BSDInstruments              /usr/sbin/bsdinstruments / bsdinstruments

The /usr/bin/fetch tool links libfetch; /usr/bin/bsdtar (with the tar symlink)
links libarchive. Shared-library consumers inherit these probes after a
normal build/install. Already statically linked consumers must be relinked.
Libraries' static archives also include provider metadata and retain anchors.
The semaphore provider shares libc's existing nameres_provider.d DOF input
and anchor: this avoids cyclic prerequisites from separate provider objects.
No public C API, shared-library version, syscall ABI or default policy changes.

USDT is conditional on MK_DTRACE=yes. Installed user providers have PID
suffixes; target the process that actually does the work. Kernel SDT requires
KDTRACE_HOOKS and the corresponding running kernel/module. A loaded old
kernel cannot acquire these probes from new profile files alone. The profile
catalog is selected by the maintained PROFILES install rule; all 17 additions
were confirmed in its 310-entry list. Existing profiles were not removed.

Qualification and reproducibility
---------------------------------
On 2026-10-13, using the native amd64 prepared GENERIC-NODEBUG object tree:
  * All 26 passes recorded edits; kernel passes compiled with hooks on/off.
  * Final kernel matrix: 32/32 translation-unit configurations passed,
    including linux64 and linux (32-bit compatibility ABI).
  * The kernel and USB, sound, NVMe, linux64, linux and LinuxKPI modules linked.
    Standalone LinuxKPI make received KERN_OPTS from prepared opt*.h files.
  * libfetch, libarchive, libthr, cp, install and libc built and linked with
    MK_DTRACE=yes and no (12 component configurations), using all 16 CPUs.
    libc/libthr use /usr/obj/usr/src/amd64.amd64/tmp as the prepared sysroot;
    installed host headers lack a current pthread constant.
  * ELF DOF inspection confirmed provider names, argument counts, nonempty
    firing offsets and is-enabled offsets in all six enabled components,
    and provider absence in their disabled counterparts.
  * Static libc semaphore consumers linked with --gc-sections retained the
    enabled semwait DOF, omitted it when disabled, and passed behavior checks.
  * All 61 definitions have call sites; 34/34 plain/filtered offline profile
    compilations passed, with argument bounds and installed catalog checked.
  * Both builds passed functional copy, FIFO fallback, safe install, digest
    install, missing-source handling, fetch data/EOF/EPIPE, archive skipping,
    timed rwlock contention and semaphore timeout/success checks (18 checks).

Run from /usr/src (validation writes to /usr/obj, never an update repository):
  python3.12 tools/test/system-tracing/coverage-fourth-compile.py \
    --kernel-obj /usr/obj/usr/src/amd64.amd64/sys/GENERIC-NODEBUG
  python3.12 tools/test/system-tracing/coverage-fourth-check.py
  python3.12 tools/test/system-tracing/coverage-fourth-dof.py
  python3.12 tools/test/system-tracing/coverage-fourth-smoke.py

The DOF and smoke tools expect the enabled/disabled build artifacts described
by the recorded build commands in pass-21.json through pass-26.json. The
profile checker verifies the recorded source snapshot, not arbitrary future
edits. Update the inventory after deliberately changing a contract/source.

Remaining live gates
--------------------
The host exposes no /dev/dtrace device. Offline compilation, ELF metadata and
ordinary execution do NOT establish that a live probe fired, measured a
correct duration, or ran with no DTrace drops/errors. Boot the matching kernel
and modules in a test VM, enumerate providers, start tracing before each
workload, assert expected counts/results, and test interruption and parallel
work. Qualify USB/audio/NVMe/PCI on suitable hardware or validated emulation;
do not trigger storage resets, low-memory pressure or PCI power transitions
on a production host merely to generate events. Confirm Linuxulator native
and compat workloads and LinuxKPI driver paths independently. Installation,
package publication, module loading, upgrading and rebooting were not done.
